@startuml activity-workshop-day
!include _style.iuml
title Activity — the workshop day (UC30, UC32–UC35, UC40–UC42)

|Workshop controller|
|Service advisor|
|Technician|
|System|
|Workshop controller|
start
:Open the day's workload
(booked minutes per bay and technician);
if (A technician is off or a bay is down?) then (yes)
  :Move the affected jobs to another bay
  or technician, with a reason;
  |System|
  :Check the bay or technician that changes: active,
  right bay type, has the skill, on shift for the whole
  job; EXCLUDE has the last word
  (busy → 409 RESOURCE_BUSY); audit row "Moved: …";
else (no)
endif
|Service advisor|
:Open the workshop day board
(bays as rows, jobs placed by time);
:Select a booking;
note left
  "Has the vehicle arrived?" is the advisor's call
  at the desk. The system does not check the date:
  a CONFIRMED job can be started on any day, also
  before the booked one (open question, code review Q1).
end note
if (Has the vehicle arrived?) then (yes)
  :Hand the vehicle to the
  assigned technician;
  |Technician|
  :Open "My jobs", read the service,
  the checklist and the customer's note;
  if (Parts needed?) then (yes)
    :Order parts for the job
    (parts staff order, receive and issue them);
  else (no)
  endif
  :Start job;
  note right: The advisor can also start it from the board.
  |System|
  :CONFIRMED → **IN_PROGRESS**;
  |Technician|
  :Do the work;
  :Job done;
  |System|
  :IN_PROGRESS → **COMPLETED**;
else (no)
  |Service advisor|
  if (Start time passed and\nthe customer did not come?) then (yes)
    :Mark no-show;
    |System|
    :CONFIRMED → **NO_SHOW**
    (bay and technician freed);
  else (no: the booking must be dropped)
    |Service advisor|
    :Cancel the booking (before work starts);
    |System|
    :CONFIRMED → **CANCELLED**
    (slot freed, a linked request re-opens);
  endif
endif
|System|
:Write the audit row (appointment_events),
log appointment.status_changed, count the metric;
note right
  Any other move (e.g. COMPLETED → IN_PROGRESS)
  → 409; a technician acting on someone else's
  job → 403. Nothing changes.
end note
stop
@enduml
